Revision history for Games-Sokoban-Solver

0.01  (not yet released)
    - First release: the solver pipeline of the Sokoban project of Jiri Broz,
      transplanted into a CPAN distribution.  Engines carried over: Firstbet 3.8
      (ten modes), Festival 0.20 (eight), Fest 1.03 (eight), FirstBack 0.07
      (one), the optimal Solver 3.3 as Games::Sokoban::Solver::Optimal, and the
      level preparation (Code 1.0, Parser 1.0, Festival_Parser 0.02, FestDev
      1.00).  Deadlock patterns are computed at run time by the Finder instead
      of being read from the project's pattern database.
    - Two things the project's engines never met and the Parser now refuses or
      reports instead: a level with a goal no box can ever be pushed onto (the
      Festival engine died on such a level), and a Festival analysis whose two
      budget fuses fired -- the hash carries hotspots_incomplete and
      envelopes_incomplete where the project stopped with an error.
    - The optimal solver keeps its three regimes (DIAL, ASTAR, FIFO) and the
      band; what went was the storage: the database writes, the BerkeleyDB seam
      (the caches live in RAM for one solve), the SQL log and the statistics.
      $LastStatus names the stop, $ON_IMPROVED reports every improvement.
    - The BerkeleyDB branch is optional: Games::Sokoban::Solver::Berkeley (the
      stores), Firstbet::Berk and Optimal::Berk (the twins that keep the search
      on disk) load only where the BerkeleyDB module is installed, under a root
      directory the caller names; a second process on one store directory is
      refused, and the optimal twin refuses a pool over 3 GB (the module keeps
      the size in 32 bits).
    - Skeleton created with h2xs 1.23 (-AX --skip-exporter --use-new-tests).
